1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,568
Welcome to the Grotta del
Bue Marino, one of the most
extraordinary places in the
Gulf of Orosei. Before
beginning the tour, it
is essential to know and
respect the visiting rules:

2
00:00:12,568 --> 00:00:24,717
they are in place to protect
you and this unique,
fragile, and millennia-old
environment. The visit will
last approximately
50 minutes. The route runs
along a single walkway,

3
00:00:24,717 --> 00:00:36,796
accessible to everyone,
covering approximately
1 kilometre on the way
in and 1 kilometre on the
way back. Pushchairs are
permitted and wheelchairs
can be used for the entire

4
00:00:36,796 --> 00:00:48,805
route. The path is linear
and has no branches open
to the public. It is,
however, very important
to respect the timing.
Within 50 minutes, you must
be back outside the cave

5
00:00:48,805 --> 00:01:01,722
in order to board the vessel
that will take you to your
next destination. For this
reason, it is essential
to keep up with the guide's
pace and not fall too far
behind. Stopping for too

6
00:01:01,722 --> 00:01:14,639
long along the route could
compromise the timing of the
visit and risk missing the
boat. By working together
and maintaining a steady
pace, everyone will be able
to enjoy the experience

7
00:01:14,639 --> 00:01:27,347
calmly and in full. The cave
is an extremely delicate
ecosystem. Do not touch the
stalactites and stalagmites:
even a simple touch can
interrupt a growth process
that takes thousands

8
00:01:27,347 --> 00:01:39,845
of years. Do not collect
anything and do not leave
any litter. Every element
here has scientific and
naturalistic value. Follow
only the walkways and the
marked route. Leaving the

9
00:01:39,845 --> 00:01:52,203
authorised areas is not
permitted. This ensures your
safety and protects the
limestone formations. Keep
your voice low. The cave
amplifies sounds, and
a quiet environment allows

10
00:01:52,203 --> 00:02:04,422
everyone to enjoy a truly
evocative and authentic
experience. Smoking is not
permitted. Open flames are
strictly forbidden.
Photography is allowed, but
the use of camera flash

11
00:02:04,422 --> 00:02:16,780
is prohibited: in addition
to potentially disturbing
the balance of the
underground environment, the
flash compromises the
quality of the visit itself.
In a naturally dark space

12
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:29,348
like the cave, sudden
artificial light alters the
atmosphere, creates strong
visual pollution, and breaks
the spell of shadows,
silence, and reflections
on the water that makes the

13
00:02:29,348 --> 00:02:41,986
experience unique. The guide
is responsible for your
safety. Listen carefully
to the instructions,
especially in the narrower
sections or where the ground
is wet. The Grotta del Bue

14
00:02:41,986 --> 00:02:52,320
Marino is a precious natural
heritage site: your respect
is an integral part of the
experience. Thank you for
your cooperation and enjoy
your visit.
